# Founder OS — enforce LF line endings everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (git's default core.autocrlf=true) delivers
# CRLF text files. The skill-catalog parser and the structural `verify` checks
# in cli/src/utils/skills.ts are line-ending sensitive — CRLF would make them
# fail on Windows while passing on Linux/macOS. Forcing LF keeps every platform
# byte-identical. (The parser also normalizes CRLF defensively, but the repo
# itself should never carry CRLF.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF or they will not run.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — git must never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
